1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:01,750
Insert Delete GetRandom O(1) — LeetCode 380

2
00:00:01,750 --> 00:00:08,250
Problem: design a set with three operations — insert adds if not present, remove deletes if present, getRandom returns a uniformly random element — and every operation must run in O(1) average time.

3
00:00:08,250 --> 00:00:10,750
Intuition: getRandom needs uniform picking, so store elements in an array; and to find values fast, use a hash map from value to index.

4
00:00:10,750 --> 00:00:15,300
But deleting from the middle of an array is O(n) — the trick: swap the target with the last element, then pop. Order doesn't matter in a set.

5
00:00:15,300 --> 00:00:18,600
insert: append to the array and record its index in the map.

6
00:00:18,600 --> 00:00:20,840
getRandom: return v at a random index — O(1).

7
00:00:20,840 --> 00:00:23,480
remove(2): the map says it's at index 1.

8
00:00:23,480 --> 00:00:26,070
Swap the last element, 3, into that slot, and update 3's index in the map.

9
00:00:26,070 --> 00:00:27,700
Pop the last slot — O(1), no shifting.

10
00:00:27,700 --> 00:00:30,540
Erase 2 from the map. Done in O(1): v = [1, 3], map = {1→0, 3→1}.

11
00:00:30,540 --> 00:00:34,680
Array for random access plus a map for O(1) lookup — insert, remove, and getRandom are all O(1).

12
